Let the weights of Abby, Bart, Cindy, and Damon be $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$, respectively. We have the equations \begin{align*}
a+b&=260\\
b+c&=245\\
c+d&=270
\end{align*} Subtracting the second equation from the first, we have $(a+b)-(b+c)=260-245 \Rightarrow a-c=15$. Adding this last equation to the third given equation, we have $(a-c)+(c+d)=15+270 \Rightarrow a+d=285$. Thus, Abby and Damon together weigh $285$ pounds.

\boxed{285}

