Let I, II, and III denote the areas of the triangles as shown on the diagram. The area of $\Delta ABC$ can be obtained by subtracting I+II+III from the area of the rectangle.

I $= 4 \times 2/2 = 4$, II $= 5 \times 2/2 = 5$, III = $1 \times 4/2 = 2$; I+II+III $= 4+5+2 = 11$.

Subtracting these areas from the area of the large rectangle tells us that the area of $ABC$ is $4\cdot 5 - 4-5-2 = 9$ square units.

