Let the number of students in Teresa's class be $a$. Then \begin{align*}
a\equiv -1\equiv 2\pmod 3,\\
a\equiv -2\equiv 2\pmod 4,\\
a\equiv -3\equiv 2\pmod 5.
\end{align*} Since $\gcd(3,4)=\gcd(4,5)=\gcd(3,5)=1$, we have $$a\equiv 2\pmod{3\cdot 4\cdot 5},$$ that is, $a\equiv 2\pmod{60}$. Since $a$ is then of the form $a=2+60n$, the only such number in the range $50<a<100$ is $62$.

