\end{align*}Squaring the first equation, we get  \[(x-y)^2=12^2\Rightarrow x^2-2xy+y^2=144\]Multiplying the second equation by four, we get $4xy = 4\cdot45=180$. Adding these last two equations, we have \[x^2-2xy+y^2+4xy=144+180 \Rightarrow (x+y)^2=324 \Rightarrow x+y = 18\]In the last step, we take the positive square root because both $x$ and $y$ are given to be positive. The sum of the two integers is $18$.

\boxed{18}

