label("$D$",D,E);
label("$E$",I,W);
draw(A--(0,0)--B,dashed);
draw((3,3)..A--B..cycle,dashed);
dot((2,1));
[/asy] Let $O=(0,0)$, $A=(0,2)$, $B=(4,0)$, $C=(2\pi+1,0)$, $D=(2\pi+1,4)$, and $E=(0,4)$. Then the area of the pentagon is $$[ABCDE]=[OCDE]-[OAB] = 4\cdot(2\pi+1)-\frac{1}{2}(2\cdot4) = 8\pi,$$and the area of the semicircle is $$\frac{1}{2}\pi(\sqrt{5})^2 = \frac{5}{2}\pi.$$The probability is $$\frac{\frac{5}{2}\pi}{8\pi} = \frac{5}{16}.$$

