dot("$Q$", Q, W);
dot("$R$", R, W);
[/asy]

Then by the triangle inequality,
\[AP + BP = QP + BP \ge BQ.\]By the Pythagorean Theorem, $BQ = \sqrt{BR^2 + QR^2} \ge BR = 6.$

Equality occurs when $P$ coincides with the intersection of line segment $\overline{BR}$ with the parabola, so the minimum value of $AP + BP$ is $6.$

