label("$4x - 3y = 30$", A + 1.5*dir(70), N);
label("$4x - 3y = 10$", -1.5*dir(70), S);

dot((0,0));
[/asy]

Solving the system $2x + y = 0$ and $4x - 3y = 10,$ we find $x = 1$ and $y = -2.$  Therefore, the center of the circle is $(1,-2).$

